Starting the first day with some basic introduction to networking .
Computer networking is the process of connecting computers and other devices so they can communicate and share data and resources.

----Networking Basics----

->Network – A group of connected devices that communicate with each other.
->LAN (Local Area Network) – A network covering a small area such as a home, school, or office.
->WAN (Wide Area Network) – A network that connects devices across large geographical areas. The Internet is the biggest example.
->IP Address – A unique logical address used to identify a device on a network.
->MAC Address – A unique hardware address assigned to a network interface.
->Router – Connects different networks and forwards packets between them.
->Switch – Connects multiple devices within a local network and forwards data to the appropriate device.
->Access Point (AP) – Allows wireless devices to connect to a wired network.
->Packet – A small unit of data transmitted across a network.
->Protocol – A set of rules that devices follow to communicate.
->Bandwidth – The maximum amount of data that can be transmitted over a connection in a given time.
->Wi-Fi – A wireless networking technology used to connect devices to a network.
->Subnet – A smaller logical division of an IP network.
->Default Gateway – The device, usually a router, that forwards traffic from one network to another.
->DNS (Domain Name System) – Converts domain names such as google.com into IP addresses.


